It is an independent implementation. No source code, prompt text, assets or
user-facing copy were taken from any other desktop assistant: the wording of
every prompt, guide and message was written for this project, and the only
third-party material is the set of libraries listed in requirements.txt, each
under its own license:

  PyQt6            GPL-3.0 / commercial (Qt Company)   - graphical interface
  sounddevice      MIT                                  - microphone, playback
  numpy            BSD-3-Clause                         - audio buffers
  faster-whisper   MIT                                  - local speech to text
  piper            MIT                                  - local text to speech

Those are optional: the core (conversation, tools, factory client) runs on the
Python standard library alone, and the interface degrades to the console when a
library is missing.

The voice commands reach "La Fabrique", a separate project distributed under the
Apache License 2.0. Nothing in that project is embedded here; it is called over
HTTP on the port the user configures.
